Title: Little Red Riding Hood
Credit: Written by
Author: Charles Perrault
Source: from the 1697 tale
Draft date: October 15, 2026

INT. MOTHER'S HOUSE - DAY

= The Mother sends her daughter to take a cake to her sick grandmother.

A village kitchen. Cakes cool on the table. LITTLE RED RIDING HOOD, a girl in a scarlet hood, plays by the door.

THE MOTHER
(filling a basket)
Go and see how your grandmother is. I hear she is ill.

LITTLE RED RIDING HOOD
Shall I take her the cake?

THE MOTHER
And this little pot of butter. Don't dawdle on the way.

The girl takes the basket and runs out.

EXT. WOODS - DAY

= The Wolf dares not eat her because of the woodcutters. She tells him where she is going.

Close-set trunks, axes ringing in the distance. Little Red Riding Hood walks along the path. THE WOLF steps out of a thicket, all smiles.

THE WOLF
Where are you going, my pretty child?

LITTLE RED RIDING HOOD
To my grandmother's, past the mill. I'm taking her a cake.

THE WOLF
(smiling)
I'll go and see her too. I'll take this path, you take that one, and we'll see who gets there first.

The Wolf runs off by the shortest path. The girl lingers, gathering hazelnuts.

INT. GRANDMOTHER'S HOUSE - DAY

= The Wolf imitates the child's voice and devours the Grandmother.

Knock, knock. THE GRANDMOTHER, in bed, turns her head toward the door.

GRANDMOTHER (V.O.)
Who's there?

THE WOLF
(imitating the girl's voice)
It's your granddaughter, Little Red Riding Hood.

GRANDMOTHER
Pull the peg, and the latch will fall.

The Wolf pulls the peg. The door opens.

CUT TO:

INT. GRANDMOTHER'S HOUSE - LATER

= "Grandmother, what big teeth you have!"

The Wolf lies in the bed, the grandmother's cap on his head. Little Red Riding Hood comes closer.

LITTLE RED RIDING HOOD
Grandmother, what big teeth you have!

THE WOLF
All the better to eat you with.
